-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 12:43:19 UTC 2026 - Dominique Leuenberger <dimstar@opensuse.org>

- Update to version 3.2:
  * Spice-webdavd: close the local client connection when the host drops it,
    instead of leaving the webdav client waiting for the end of the response or
    reusing a dropped connection, which led to dropped frames and hangs
  * Spice-webdavd: announce the local mDNS service on loopback only, and run as
    an unprivileged user in the systemd unit
  * Libphodav: add debug tracing for the request lifecycle, the streamed
    response pulls and the spice mux frames, silent unless G_MESSAGES_DEBUG is
    set
  * Windows testing fixes: read the virtual-dir server port from a file to
    avoid the carriage return of the text-mode standard handles, and run the
    Wine tests with their output to regular files, which a stray "explorer.exe
    /desktop" process cannot keep open
  * Updated translations.
- Changes from version 3.1:
  * CVE-2026-114417: reject the encoded slashes in the COPY/MOVE
    Destination header, which allowed writing outside of the shared directory
  * CVE-2026-114418: don't handle PUT when the request was already rejected:
    with digest authentication configured, an unauthenticated client could
    create or overwrite any file of the share
  * CVE-2026-114419: chezdav: check the digest password, any password was
    accepted for a user listed in the htdigest file
  * refuse the oversized request bodies with 413, including the chunked ones,
    and don't run the method handler of an already rejected request
  * fix crash and hangs on invalid If headers
  * fix a crash on PROPFIND/PROPPATCH requests without any property
- Update version dependencies according to meson.build.
- Drop harden_spice-webdavd.service.patch: fixed upstream.
- Convert to _service for easier management.
- Replace gtk-doc BuildRequires for scdoc and pkgconfig(gi-docgen): follow
  upstreams port away from gtk-doc
- Add pkgconfig(neon), pkgconfig(gobject-introspection-1.0): new dependencies
- Split out lang files from the shared library package: fixing policy violation
- Provide phodav-3.0 by the libphodav-3_0-0 to have the new lang package
  installable

